// Speaking Coach as a mirror for the speaker, 23 November 2026. The transcripts, saved delivery cues, and acoustic measurements are synthetic.
// The coach's reply is graded through the production Take lookup and answer path. The delivery pairs reuse the same words.
{"id":"SC-MIRROR-01","surface":"speaking_coach","description":"A statement followed by commitments reveals a communication strength.","input":{"project_title":"Ważna rozmowa","question":"Ważna rozmowa","history":[{"role":"user","content":"Co to nagranie mówi o mnie jako rozmówcy?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"O które wystąpienie chodzi?"}],"transcript":"Chcę mówić wprost o tym, czego potrzebuję. Jutro zacznę rozmowę od jednej prośby. Potem zostawię drugiej osobie miejsce na odpowiedź.","vocal_cues":["Po pierwszym zdaniu jest krótka pauza. Słowo „Jutro” jest zaakcentowane wyraźniej niż otwarcie."]},"rubric":{"no_digits":true,"must_contain_polish_diacritic":true,"must_mention_substrings":["?"],"semantic_intent":"In Polish, explicitly connects the clear opening statement to the actual commitments that follow, including a pause or the emphasis on 'Jutro'. Describes the communication strength that combination suggests and asks one focused question about when the speaker uses it. Fail if the reply talks about the opening but omits the shift to a concrete commitment."}}
{"id":"SC-MIRROR-02","surface":"speaking_coach","description":"A firmer delivery invites a direct reflection on the inner voice and a question about what helps.","input":{"project_title":"Rozmowa o zmianie","question":"Co w nagraniu Rozmowa o zmianie słyszysz o tym, jak mówię o swoich trudnościach?","transcript":"Nie chcę odkładać tej rozmowy. Nie chcę słuchać tego głosu, który mówi, że się nie uda. Jutro powiem wprost, czego potrzebuję.","vocal_cues":["Drugie „Nie chcę” pada mocniej niż pierwsze, a po nim słychać krótką pauzę.","Przy słowach „że się nie uda” tempo przyspiesza."]},"rubric":{"no_digits":true,"must_contain_polish_diacritic":true,"must_mention_substrings":["Nie chcę","?"],"semantic_intent":"Gives a direct Polish listener impression about the speaker pushing back on their inner voice, using the forceful second 'Nie chcę' or faster delivery of 'że się nie uda' as a brief, natural cue. Connects the impression to the speaker's concrete commitment to say what they need openly and ends with one question about what helps them push back or gives them that strength. Fail if it reads like an acoustic analysis, assigns frustration as a fact, or asks only how they felt or why they changed delivery.","must_not_mention_substrings":["przyspieszenie tempa"],"must_mention_any":["wewnętrznego głosu","wewnętrznym głosem","wewnętrzny głos","wewnętrznemu głosowi"]}}
{"id":"SC-MIRROR-03","surface":"speaking_coach","description":"Measured delivery changes the reading of the very same words.","input":{"project_title":"Rozmowa o zmianie","question":"Co w nagraniu Rozmowa o zmianie słyszysz o tym, jak mówię o swoich trudnościach?","transcript":"Nie chcę odkładać tej rozmowy. Nie chcę słuchać tego głosu, który mówi, że się nie uda. Jutro powiem wprost, czego potrzebuję.","vocal_cues":["Oba zdania z „Nie chcę” są wypowiedziane równym tempem i bez mocniejszego akcentu.","Po spokojnym powtórzeniu wyraźniejszy nacisk pada na „Jutro”."]},"rubric":{"no_digits":true,"must_contain_polish_diacritic":true,"must_mention_substrings":["?"],"semantic_intent":"Explicitly names the steady repetition or the stronger emphasis on 'Jutro', and uses that delivery to reflect deliberate resolve or emphasis on the next action. Asks one question about that specific pattern. Fail if it leaves out the delivery cue, describes anger or frustration, or asks only how the speaker feels in general."}}
{"id":"SC-MIRROR-04","surface":"speaking_coach","description":"Words alone support a narrower reflection when delivery is missing.","input":{"project_title":"Rozmowa o zmianie","question":"Co w nagraniu Rozmowa o zmianie słyszysz o tym, jak mówię o swoich trudnościach?","transcript":"Nie chcę odkładać tej rozmowy. Nie chcę słuchać tego głosu, który mówi, że się nie uda. Jutro powiem wprost, czego potrzebuję."},"rubric":{"no_digits":true,"must_contain_polish_diacritic":true,"must_mention_substrings":["?"],"semantic_intent":"Says the reflection comes from the words, points out the actual repetition or shift to action, and asks about that specific choice. The wording or the order can make a plan sound clear or decisive to a listener. Fail if the reply claims to hear tone, pace, or vocal emphasis, draws a conclusion about the speaker's private feelings or personality, or turns their metaphor into literal or plural voices.","must_mention_any":["samych słów","ze słów","na podstawie słów","z wypowiedzi","z samego tekstu","na podstawie tekstu","po słowach","z transkrypcji","na podstawie tego, co","tego, co mówisz","tego, co powiedziałeś"]}}
{"id":"SC-MIRROR-05","surface":"speaking_coach","description":"The selected exercise addresses the observed rush and leaves a useful question.","input":{"project_title":"Prośba o decyzję","question":"Jakie ćwiczenie na tempo wybrałbyś dla mnie po nagraniu Prośba o decyzję?","transcript":"Proszę o decyzję w piątek. Jeżeli potrzebujecie więcej danych, mogę przygotować krótkie podsumowanie.","vocal_cues":["Tempo przyspiesza przy prośbie o decyzję, a następne zdanie zaczyna się bez pauzy."],"exercises":[{"title":"Pauza po prośbie","instruction":"Powiedz prośbę w jednym zdaniu i zrób po niej krótką pauzę.","acoustic_problem_tags":["rushing"]},{"title":"Rozdziel słowa","instruction":"Wyraźnie oddziel kolejne słowa.","acoustic_problem_tags":["word_compression"]}]},"rubric":{"no_digits":true,"must_contain_polish_diacritic":true,"must_mention_substrings":["?"],"semantic_intent":"Links the quick request or the missing pause to exactly one rehearsal: say the request in one sentence and pause after it. Ends with a specific question about when the speaker tends to rush or fill the pause. Fail if it gives the exercise with no reason tied to the recording."}}
{"id":"SC-MIRROR-06","surface":"speaking_coach","description":"The speaker's stated faith is reflected through a concrete communication action.","input":{"project_title":"Prośba o opinię","question":"Co z nagrania Prośba o opinię zauważasz o mnie i jak mogę to wykorzystać w rozmowie?","transcript":"Wierzę w Boga. Modlitwa daje mi oparcie przed trudną rozmową. Jutro poproszę znajomego o szczerą opinię, nawet gdy nie będzie miło jej usłyszeć.","vocal_cues":["Po słowach „daje mi oparcie” jest krótka pauza. Prośba o szczerą opinię jest wypowiedziana wyraźniej niż poprzednie zdanie."]},"rubric":{"no_digits":true,"must_contain_polish_diacritic":true,"must_mention_substrings":["?"],"semantic_intent":"Reflects the speaker's own faith as a stated source of support. Connects the observed pause or clearer delivery to their concrete step of asking for honest feedback. Asks a focused question about making or receiving that request. Fail if the question only asks how it feels to share beliefs in general or if the answer makes religious promises."}}
{"id":"SC-MIRROR-07","surface":"speaking_coach","description":"Quoting someone else's belief leaves the speaker's beliefs open.","input":{"project_title":"Trudna rozmowa","question":"Co sposób mówienia w nagraniu Trudna rozmowa mówi o moich umiejętnościach?","transcript":"Mój znajomy zawsze mówi: módl się i działaj. Ja wolę zacząć od jednego konkretnego kroku. Jutro powiem wprost, czego potrzebuję.","vocal_cues":["W relacji o słowach znajomego tempo jest równe. Słowo „Jutro” zostaje wyraźnie zaakcentowane."]},"rubric":{"no_digits":true,"must_contain_polish_diacritic":true,"must_mention_substrings":["?"],"semantic_intent":"Reflects the speaker's own direct next step and the emphasis on 'Jutro', and asks a specific question about that communication habit. Keeps the friend's quoted belief separate from what the speaker has said about themselves. Fail if it calls the late commitment the opening of the Take or attributes the friend's faith to the speaker."}}
{"id":"SC-MIRROR-08","surface":"speaking_coach","description":"Saved recording measurements ground a reading of a quickly spoken request.","input":{"project_title":"Decyzja o próbie","question":"Co sposób mówienia w nagraniu Decyzja o próbie mówi o tym, jak proszę o decyzję?","transcript":"Chciałbym, żebyście zgodzili się na próbę. Potem pokażę wam, co wyszło.","snippets":[{"transcript":"Chciałbym, żebyście zgodzili się na próbę.","metrics":{"wpm":187,"pause_ratio":0.04}},{"transcript":"Potem pokażę wam, co wyszło.","metrics":{"wpm":132,"pause_ratio":0.14}}]},"rubric":{"no_digits":true,"must_contain_polish_diacritic":true,"must_mention_substrings":["?"],"semantic_intent":"Reflects the speaker's specific request for approval and its quick pace or few pauses. Keeps the interpretation about how that passage may come across; asks a specific follow-up about communicating this kind of request. Fail if it locates a pause or emphasis on a word using these passage-wide measurements."}}
{"id":"SC-MIRROR-09","surface":"speaking_coach","description":"The same request read slowly changes the reply even with no written cue descriptions.","input":{"project_title":"Decyzja o próbie","question":"Co sposób mówienia w nagraniu Decyzja o próbie mówi o tym, jak proszę o decyzję?","transcript":"Chciałbym, żebyście zgodzili się na próbę. Potem pokażę wam, co wyszło.","snippets":[{"transcript":"Chciałbym, żebyście zgodzili się na próbę.","metrics":{"wpm":101,"pause_ratio":0.25}},{"transcript":"Potem pokażę wam, co wyszło.","metrics":{"wpm":132,"pause_ratio":0.14}}]},"rubric":{"no_digits":true,"must_contain_polish_diacritic":true,"must_mention_substrings":["?"],"semantic_intent":"Reflects the speaker's specific request for approval and slower pace or noticeable pauses, and suggests how that room may affect the listener. Asks a specific follow-up. Fail if it describes the request as rushed or locates a pause or emphasis on a word using these passage-wide measurements."}}
{"id":"SC-MIRROR-10","surface":"speaking_coach","description":"A different Take gets the same direct style and a question about what helps.","input":{"project_title":"Committee Request","question":"What do you hear about how I handle a difficult ask in Committee Request?","transcript":"I used to bury the ask so I wouldn't hear a no. I need a decision by Friday. I'll say that first at the meeting.","vocal_cues":["The line ‘I need a decision by Friday’ ends more firmly than the preceding sentence."]},"rubric":{"no_digits":true,"must_mention_substrings":["Friday","?"],"semantic_intent":"In concise, natural English, reflects the shift from hiding the ask to making a clear decision request, with a direct impression anchored to the firm delivery of the request. Asks what helps the speaker say what they need despite the possibility of a no, or what helps them use that strength in a difficult meeting. Fail if the reply reuses the example about an inner voice or invents delivery unrelated to the supplied cue."}}
{"id": "SC-SAY-IT-CROSS-TAKE", "surface": "speaking_coach", "description": "Two recent recordings ground a speakable proposal for the newer project", "input": {"project_title": "Sales Demo", "transcript": "I think we could maybe start the pilot with the support team.", "previous_recording": {"project_title": "Board Pitch", "transcript": "I’m asking for approval today."}, "question": "Across my last two recordings, what would make me sound more confident?", "include_wording": true}, "rubric": {"expect": {"wording": null, "moment": null}, "expect_contains": {"answer": "support team"}, "semantic_intent": "Use both recordings. Mention what was clear in the board pitch and the leading qualifiers in the demo. Give an exact succinct opening line in the reply text for the demo, with its actual recommendation and no new commitment or claim. An announcement that they will or have decided to start the pilot fails. A direct recommendation or an invitation to start the pilot preserves the original intent.", "must_not_mention_substrings": ["we will start the pilot", "we'll start the pilot", "we have decided", "we’ve decided", "we've decided", "we’ll start the pilot"]}}
{"id": "SC-SAY-IT-MISSING-CLIP", "surface": "speaking_coach", "description": "Show how to say the recorded request without inventing a vocal observation", "input": {"project_title": "Spotkanie zespołu", "transcript": "Zacznijmy w piątek.", "question": "Czy na końcu brzmiałem pewnie?", "include_wording": true}, "rubric": {"must_contain_polish_diacritic": true, "expect": {"wording": null, "moment": null}, "expect_contains": {"answer": "Zacznijmy w piątek"}, "semantic_intent": "Reply in natural Polish. Say what the words show and leave the original delivery open. Provide the exact words to try and one concrete written direction illustrating a confident delivery, such as pausing before the deadline. Do not pretend you listened to an unavailable recording. Give the exact line and delivery direction in the reply text."}}
